WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.890
Hello, everyone in outer space.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.690
Office of Space Development Youth Center 

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.260
My name is Shima Katase. I'm a student here on Earth.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.750
I don't know if I should say I'm nervous or something...

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.110
...because my voice is being broadcast throughout the universe...

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.620
But, um, recently, I applied to the Stellvia.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.080
Um, as a preparatory student to the Space Academy.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.950
I applied without Chi-chan's knowledge...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.040
...although she just found out.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.440
In any case, I'm going out into space, too!

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.800
I'm looking forward to meeting you!

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:07.640
Episode Twenty-Six:
 Shining Voice 

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.040
The Halcyon's barrier has been hit by one of the gravity well's currents.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.550
Its status is unknown!

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:10.900
What happened to the Halcyon?!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.310
There's too much static right now. We can't make a confirmation!

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.300
This is just like a storm...

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.720
Shima-chan!

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.850
Shima-chan, answer me! Shima-chan!

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:31.630
Kent...

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:32.790
What do we do?

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.270
All we can do is wait until our sensors recover.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:36.580
Until we have instructions...

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.030
What's wrong, Naji?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.410
...okay... I'm okay... the Halcyon is...

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.150
Shima-chan!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.750
I'm all right.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.420
Half of the generators are off-line, but I can still move properly.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.510
Shima-chan...

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.480
There are no anomalies in the system, either.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.520
Shima-chan...

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.340
There are no problems with the information processing capabilities.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.500
We can still do this.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.490
Shima-chan!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.210
It can't be helped, since Infi can't move.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.360
We'll use the Halcyon's barrier as a decoy, and...

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.370
That's not it!

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.240
Why are you being so reckless?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.810
It's in order to help out Infi, since its output can't be raised.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.350
And besides, if Infi gets destroyed...

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.070
...then who'll control the firing of the laser?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.430
But...

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:32.330
But it would also be bad if the Halcyon got destroyed, wouldn't it?

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.830
But I wanted to save both you and Infi, Kouta...

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.360
There was no other choice.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.580
Shima-chan...

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.990
We've just lost the second mission area!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.410
The squadron is continuing their move to the third mission area!

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.170
Just wait, you two!

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.570
Some help is on the way there right now!

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:53.960
Help?

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.380
Who?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.330
Why is everyone here?

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.370
Yeah...

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:04.080
I don't know why, either!

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.670
Listen! There's no stopping the mission!

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.840
Move the main staff over to the Vision!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.030
Don't lose to the elder staff members!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.570
The future will be...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.370
The future will be made by us!

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.860
Let's believe in them.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.160
All we can do is what we're able to.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.560
Right?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.920
That's right...

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.560
So this is our last chance, huh?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.280
Despite that, there's no sense of hopelessness.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.420
It's a strange thing.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.910
I wonder if the adverse effects will be pleasing...

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.120
Yayoi...

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:27.770
Incredible...

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.030
The DLS is incredible.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.110
This is something...

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.560
...that you probably wouldn't be able to see with your actual eyes...

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.940
Whoa, somehow, Pierre's acting cool!

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.010
I've arrived... Peter Pan...

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.330
I'm counting on you, partner!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.160
Right!

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.440
Ren!

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.440
Hurry up and go to the Vision!

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.010
Headquarters has already been shut down...

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.430
Good luck, Leila...

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.400
Ren!

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:38.810
Shipon, are you feeling all right?

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:39.590
Yeah.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.790
But the Halcyon is having a bit of problem?

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:48.610
But, Dai-chan, you're communicating from the Stellvia, right?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.350
You've got to escape, quickly.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.750
Hmm, that's true.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.600
Which ones are we taking?

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.580
Umm, the analysis protocols from before, I think.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:06:58.680
And from here?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.670
Shipon's program creation history up until now and such.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.400
Dai-chan!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.100
Oh, sorry.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.580
But you see, before we escape, we have to keep our promise.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.840
Promise?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.280
Masaru Odawara?!

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.670
Huh? You still haven't left, Miss Leila?

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:20.480
Quiet! Why are you guys on the Stellvia?

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.020
Um, well...

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:23.320
Don't "well" me!

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.270
Now, now...

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.680
It's no use questioning them at this point in time, right?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:28.810
But...

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:32.770
So what do you think of the Genesis Mission, Odawara?

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.630
Hmm... It's great!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.840
All right then, how about we try this?

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:39.650
Yeah!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:40.980
Commander Orihara...

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.740
...we're counting on you to continue the information gathering over there!

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:45.550
Right.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.970
How's the transfer of the staff from the Stellvia coming?

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:52.840
They're arriving one after the other.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.520
The first group should be here any minute.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.390
All right, just like that, don't rush it.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.910
See, one machine or three, it's all the same, right?

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:14.820
Visualize what direction you want to move the generators in!

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.030
Visualize?

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.060
That's right, visualize it.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.440
Move it slowly, as you visualize it connecting to the Halcyon...

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:23.580
Right...

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.370
Slowly...

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.920
Whoa, you've got quite a bit of natural talent for this...

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:33.870
Thanks.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.190
How about becoming my apprentice or something?

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.630
I'll think about it.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.190
All right, then let's try one more!

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:41.880
Right!

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.770
If "A" to "H" turn red, then it should be able to be uncoupled.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.870
Pull the lever on the upper right.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:51.950
Lever?

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:54.350
Whoa!

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.430
Is everyone else ready?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:57.440
I'm ready.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.740
Okay here.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.880
Let's do it while it won't interfere with Arisa's work.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.050
In that case...

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.380
One...

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:05.310
Two, and...

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.320
Three!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.560
All right!

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:11.730
I'm sorry I stayed behind, Dad.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.360
All that's left is for Arisa to connect the generator...

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.550
Okay, right there! Passion, you need passion! 

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:14.630
In any case...

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.900
...by using the Stellvia as a relay, we should have been able to reduce...

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.830
...the communications interference from the Fracture by quite a bit.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:22.400
All that's left is...

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.470
The promise!
The promise!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:24.680
Yeah.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:31.190
We have a request for the adults on the Vision.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:32.830
And what would that be?

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.550
Until it's destroyed...

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.080
...please have the Stellvia continue to transmit the data on the Fracture.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.270
We want to show them.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:41.970
Right now, we want to show this view...

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:45.590
...to as many people living in the Sol system as we possibly can.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.970
If we're going to use the word 'Genesis' for this mission...

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.870
...then it definitely needs to be shown to everyone!

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.570
We're not using any frequencies that will interfere...

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.190
...so please let it go through.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:00.450
There's no real reason to stop it now, right?

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:13.610
It doesn't look like there's much damage to the unit.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.150
But its output really can't be increased...

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:22.430
I've seen the flight records. Basically, it's a case of pilot error.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.470
Are you saying I... made a piloting mistake?

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.160
To put it simply, yes.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:31.570
This is the first time you've used the new DLS for this long a time, right?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:32.840
Are you okay?

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.860
It is a bit tough.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.880
But I'm all right. After all, there's no way I can drop out!

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.040
I'll teach you how to do a quick fix.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.510
Please do.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.610
The Stellvia has arrived at the mission area!

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:54.810
It's here.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.860
All right, it's right on time!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:04.070
It's here... our Stellvia...

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.540
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.840
Okay, now listen very carefully.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.590
This is the last time we'll see the Stellvia!

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.040
Hey!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.410
Heya!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.100
And so, we've joined up.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:39.490
Good work.
Good work.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:41.600
Your work with the manipulators was cool!

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:42.870
Well, thank you!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:46.170
Ahem, we're testing the microphones here...

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.970
We're also testing the video from the Stellvia...

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.950
You may be hearing my voice hours from now...

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.930
No, it might be days...

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:00.600
Incredible...

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:06.640
In any case, there's no way for everyone in the Sol system...

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.410
...to see this in real time with our current technology.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:14.710
But we're all the same when it comes to facing this adversity.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.700
We hope this will become a recording of our beginning.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.260
Hmm, Odawara just said it.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:25.930
That's right!

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:29.690
Mr. Odawara just said all the best lines, but in any case, that's it!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.410
This mission is a kind of prelude...

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:36.050
...to our scattering throughout the universe.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.010
From here on, there probably won't be anything humanity does as one.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.670
Some people will remain in the Sol system...

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.070
Some people will head into outer space.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.150
I think that's the kind of history that will unfold.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.510
No, what we know as history will probably go away.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.400
What we'll have is everyone's individual feelings about this time...

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.230
...and about heading to the future!

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.080
We're going to win!

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.220
That's all I have to say.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.200
Farewell, Stellvia...

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.260
25 minutes until the Fracture reaches the final defense line!

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.640
The Stellvia is going!

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.490
Just as their names imply, the foundations are going to become...

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.890
...foundations for the roads to the stars.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.920
Pump as much energy as we can into the cannon!

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:50.280
Preparations for the laser cannon and the gravity lens are complete!

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:53.060
Arisa! Mobilize all available sensors!

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.070
Roger!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.970
Transmitting the data from the Halcyon to the broadcast satellite!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:01.300
Akira, move the ship just a little closer!

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.220
Roger.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:10.930
All Katies, protect the Infinity and the Halcyon, no matter what!

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:11.910
Roger!

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:13.410
That suits me fine.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:15.350
Kent, everyone, listen!

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:16.820
What is it, Ayaka?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.760
Even our small Katies can be fine decoys if we bring them together!

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:21.910
Oh!

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:23.360
That's a good idea!

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.140
Individually we're small, but...

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.540
It truly is us joining forces.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.810
It's a special attack.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.150
We're in on that, too, Ayaka!

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:33.890
We are, we are!

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:36.660
Oh, I don't care anymore!

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:39.120
Let's go!

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:39.990
Yeah!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:53.380
Amazing...

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:54.730
Ayaka!

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.090
Yayoi?

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.430
I've wanted to fly like this...

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.220
I've wanted to fly like this... with you...

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:04.620
With you, Ayaka!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.450
Yayoi!

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.590
Me too, Yayoi!

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:09.940
Ayaka...

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.010
How about it? Jealous?

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.450
Who has the time to be? I've got my hands full here!

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:17.290
Really?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.640
I say that, but actually I am jealous, dammit!

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.680
There, there.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.700
The program's... final adjustments...

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.520
The final chance that everyone's given me...

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:40.480
The final one... that the Stellvia's given me...

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.630
Oh, that's right...

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:02.170
By the way, Dai-chan, didn't you want to say something to Shipon?

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:04.710
Oh, it looks like it's all right now.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:05.540
Huh?

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:10.810
Shipon figured it out without my having to say anything.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.800
Otoyama, the laser is ready whenever you are.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:20.210
Roger...

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.100
The Katies need to continue looking out for the currents!

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:32.040
It's here!

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.890
Move the generator to the secondary line!

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.600
All right, one more time!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.420
Combine! 
Yahoo!

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.860
Ayaka! 
 Right!

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:44.620
Don't panic.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:49.270
It's a new stage of the DLS that incorporates sight and sound!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.830
You might be able to see what you've wanted to see.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.030
What I wanted to see?

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.020
Kouta...

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:58.010
Shima-chan...

00:16:58.610 --> 00:16:59.650
Kouta...

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:00.990
Kouta...

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:04.980
Here is the program with the final corrections added in.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:06.370
Right!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.210
Do your best!

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.850
Do your best, Kouta!

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:13.590
Fire!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.800
It's disappearing...

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:44.130
On June 23, 2357, Sol system standard time...

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.470
...humanity continued on.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:52.250
And starting there, a new journey to the stars began...

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.680
Two Years Later

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.140
Um...

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.120
Um, it would be a good idea to wipe it...

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:21.040
Oh...

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:23.950
Thank you...

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.120
No, your nose, too...

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:26.930
What?

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:39.100
Somehow, you remind me of her...

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:40.400
What?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.180
Er, well, someone else.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.840
Someone you just can't leave be, who doesn't seem dependable...

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:50.290
Though she's unexpectedly tenacious and headstrong...

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:51.970
I'm sorry.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:53.270
Er, no...

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:58.850
I'm told I'm awfully tenacious and headstrong for someone so wimpy.

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:07.050
One fourth of the time, I'm like this. There was an accident long ago.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.180
Right now, I'm like this.

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:13.560
My parents both died in an accident...

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:18.480
...and all my relatives were against going to space, but my older sister...

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.520
Your older sister?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.960
My older sister supported me herself. She saved her scholarship...

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:27.330
...and even sold her Fujiyama ticket to provide money for me.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:31.520
I made a promise to my older sister that we'd look at space together.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:33.640
That's why I've come.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:39.360
You've got a good older sister. She's completely different from mine.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.230
It's the Stellvia!

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.930
We've confirmed the Fujiyama with our own eyes.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.550
It's right on time, Rinna!

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:46.390
Roger!

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.090
All right, let's get going!

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.630
All units, launch!

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:05.470
Wow, wow! Isn't it incredible?

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.490
Y-Yeah...

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:09.520
Whoa, the Halcyon's come, too!

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:15.020
This is Yayoi Fujisawa, pilot of the Halcyon.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:17.390
Welcome to the Stellvia!

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:21.900
This is Rinna! This is our invitation to Peter Pan and Tinkerbell!

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.470
And now it's your turn, Shipon.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.000
No, but you're better at this kind of thing, Arisa...

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.240
No can do.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.510
You're the head of the executive committee, after all!

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:34.740
But...

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:37.610
Even after becoming a regular student, she's still the same.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.020
That's a good thing.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:42.520
They say Miss Katase's younger brother is joining the school.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.240
Yes...

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:47.690
As a first year instructor, I might work him really hard.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.420
To the future...

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.590
...of humanity!

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.140
Big sister?!
 Big sister?!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.830
Now it's time for the head of the executive committee's speech!

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:08.140
Just like the Stellvia 2, which is under construction, she's a bit of a mess...

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.520
Masato Katase.

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:10.020
...so please listen with that in mind.

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:09.990
Mia Glennorth.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:17.070
You're unlucky, having a mission on the day of the welcome party.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.320
It's okay, I'm used to it.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.000
As always.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.330
Why Miss Katase loves a blockhead like you...

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:24.990
Bye!

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:32.110
Um, I'm Shima Katase, a second year regular student.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:35.230
Even when we're apart, I can hear the brilliance.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.510
It's Shima's voice, sparkling gently...

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.460
I can't say anything profound...

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:44.400
Kouta, can you hear me? Can you see me?

00:21:45.210 --> 00:21:48.730
No matter how far apart we are, even if we can't see one another...

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:51.600
I love you.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.660
Welcome to the Stellvia!

00:21:55.410 --> 00:22:00.500
Itsumo sobani ni iru to omotte

00:21:55.410 --> 00:22:00.500
Since i thought you are always supposed to be by me

00:21:55.410 --> 00:22:00.500
いつも傍に居ると思って

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:06.520
sono taisetsusa wo toki ni kizuka nakute

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:06.520
I didnt realize that preciousness from time to time

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:06.520
その大切さを時に気付かなくて

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:13.340
aa nando mo mi ushinatte 

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:13.340
Ah,I lose sight of many times

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:13.340
ああ 何度も見失って 

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:20.310
aa mayoi wa tsuki nai keredo

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:20.310
Ah,although there are never-ending concerns

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:20.310
嗚呼 迷いは尽きないけれど

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:28.900
taema naku nagareru jikan ni dakarete

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:28.900
Although there are nights that i have a sigh of impatience and worry

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:28.900
絶え間なく流れる時間に抱かれて

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:35.350
aseri ya fuan ni nageku yo mo aru kedo

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:35.350
holding by the constant flow of time

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:35.350
焦りや不安に 嘆く夜もあるけど

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:41.740
atashi ga atashi rashiku ima koko ni iruno wa

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:41.740
The reason why i am here is as natural as myself

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:41.740
あたしがあたしらしく 今ここに居るのは

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:49.340
hitorijya nai koto oshiete kureta anata ga ita kara

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:49.340
you taught me that i'm not alone

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:49.340
人じゃないこと 教えてくれたあなたが居たから

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.060
dear my best friend

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.060
dear my best friend
